// An UN-ANNOTATED (hole) parameter loses the `is` COMPLEMENT narrowing its annotated twin
// has. `if a is "err" { … } else { … }` narrows the HIT arm at both faces; only the else arm
// differs, and `vl check` refuses with `operator '*' is not defined for i32 | "err" and i32`.
// The annotated twin — the same body under `function take(a: i32 | "err")` — prints 10, so
// the program is type-valid and the refusal is clause 2.
// Found 2026-09-02 by the position-matrix harness at `argument` / `early_return_guard`.
// See D1243.
// Should print 10.
function orErr(bad: boolean): i32 | "err" {
  if bad { return "err" }
  return 5
}

function take(a) {
  if a is "err" { print(0) } else { print(a * 2) }
}

take(orErr(false))
